<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>If I recall correctly, the intelligent culture of SCP-1000 has long been destroyed, leaving them much simpler than they were before humans wiped their minds. Russia has been a communist country for a relatively short time. This skip references a &quot;red army officer,&quot; so I assume he's talking about the communist army. How could that be if SCP-1000 has long since been wiped out, memory wise?</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p>Other than that mild confusion (which is probably just me failing to pick up a detail or five), great article, fantastic writing, and good job!</p>

